## Promotion Rule

Promote a candidate into an ADR when at least one of these is true:

- implementation would be materially different depending on the outcome
- multiple reasonable options exist
- the decision crosses module or system boundaries
- the decision will be hard to reverse after implementation begins

## Deleting An ADR

If review shows an ADR never actually recorded a decision — it duplicates the ground rules, or the decision it describes is already fully specified elsewhere — delete it rather than leaving it as clutter. Note the deletion and the reason in this index or the CHANGELOG so the missing number isn't mistaken for an accident.

## Retiring An ADR

When an ADR is fully superseded, move its body to [../archive/](../archive/) and leave a short stub at the original path pointing to the current authority document and the archive copy. This keeps existing inbound links resolving instead of breaking, and stops a reader from mistaking a retired decision for current behavior.

Update this index's `Status` column to `superseded`, linking to whatever replaced it.
